 @milkrxllz  >he still thinks it's a joke
let me spell something out for you: there's edgy humor and then there's 'edgy humor'. the second one is where you tell people exactly who you are and what you believe and you laugh at how they'll try to rationalize it because they don't want to admit to themselves that they've just witnessed evil unmasked.
Max Frisch wrote a short play about this, 'the fire raisers', which might help you wrap your head around it. C.S. Lewis also gets into this stuff.
